### Metrics Delta Analysis (vs BM25 Baseline)

- **`+dense` (No Fusion)**
  - **Recall@50**: +0.1272
  - **NDCG@10**: +0.0817
  - **MRR@10**: +0.0572
  - **p95 Latency**: +84.0 ms 
  - *Analysis*: With the full index, Dense retrieval strictly dominates BM25 across all accuracy metrics. It pushed candidate recall up by an absolute 12.7%, bringing over 63% of relevant products into the top-50 pool.

- **`+hybrid` (RRF)**
  - **Recall@50**: +0.1243
  - **NDCG@10**: +0.1022
  - **MRR@10**: +0.0913
  - **p95 Latency**: +91.6 ms
  - *Analysis*: RRF successfully capitalizes on both candidate pools. While Recall@50 stays effectively the same as dense (since dense already retrieved the majority of relevant candidates), the hybrid fusion dramatically improves ranking quality at the top (NDCG@10 hits 0.5180 and MRR@10 jumps to 0.7538). The p95 latency is extremely healthy at **279.6 ms**, comfortably below the 800 ms budget thanks to concurrent asyncio execution.

